CAT = "phnatReading"; SEG = "RDG"
# Four original passages, four questions each. The passage is embedded in every stem.
P1 = "Read the passage: \"Handwashing is one of the simplest ways to stop the spread of infection. Germs picked up from doorknobs, money and phones travel on the hands to the mouth, nose and eyes. Washing with soap and running water for at least twenty seconds loosens dirt and germs so they rinse away. Water alone removes far fewer germs. When soap and water are not available, an alcohol-based hand rub is a useful substitute, although it does not work well on hands that are visibly dirty.\""
P2 = "Read the passage: \"Florence Nightingale arrived at a British army hospital in 1854 and found wounded soldiers lying in filthy, crowded wards. More men were dying of fever and infection than of battle wounds. She had the wards scrubbed, opened the windows, and improved the food and the water supply. Within months the death rate fell sharply. Nightingale kept careful records and used charts to persuade officials that clean conditions save lives. Her work helped turn nursing into a respected profession.\""
P3 = "Read the passage: \"Dengue is spread by the bite of the Aedes mosquito, which breeds in clean, standing water. Old tires, flower vases, and uncovered drums around the home are common breeding sites. The mosquito bites mostly in the early morning and late afternoon. Because no medicine kills the virus, treatment focuses on rest, fluids, and watching for warning signs such as severe stomach pain and bleeding gums. The most effective protection is still to search for and destroy the places where mosquitoes lay their eggs.\""
P4 = "Read the passage: \"Sleep is not wasted time. While a person sleeps, the brain sorts the day's experiences and stores what is worth keeping. Students who sleep well after studying usually remember more than those who stay up all night. Lack of sleep also slows reaction time and weakens the body's defenses against illness. Most teenagers need eight to ten hours each night, yet many get far less because of late-night screen use. Putting gadgets away an hour before bedtime helps the body settle into sleep.\""
Q = [
(P1 + " What is the main idea of the passage?",
 "Proper handwashing prevents infection", ["Germs are found on money and phones", "Hand rubs are better than soap", "Dirty hands need longer washing"],
 "Every sentence supports the opening point that handwashing stops the spread of infection. Germs on money is only a supporting detail."),
(P1 + " According to the passage, how do germs on the hands enter the body?",
 "Through the mouth, nose and eyes", ["Through cuts on the fingers", "Through the skin of the palms", "Through food that is shared"],
 "The passage says germs travel on the hands to the mouth, nose and eyes. Cuts and shared food are not mentioned."),
(P1 + " When is an alcohol-based hand rub least effective?",
 "When hands are visibly dirty", ["When soap is also available", "When used for twenty seconds", "When hands are completely dry"],
 "The last sentence says the hand rub does not work well on hands that are visibly dirty."),
(P1 + " As used in the passage, what does \"substitute\" mean?",
 "replacement", ["improvement", "medicine", "requirement"],
 "The hand rub is used in place of soap and water when they are not available, so it is a replacement."),
(P2 + " What was killing most of the soldiers in the hospital?",
 "Fever and infection", ["Battle wounds", "Lack of surgeons", "Cold weather"],
 "The passage says more men were dying of fever and infection than of battle wounds."),
(P2 + " Which change did Nightingale make in the wards?",
 "She had them cleaned and aired", ["She moved them near the battle", "She closed them to visitors", "She filled them with more beds"],
 "She had the wards scrubbed and opened the windows. The wards were already crowded, so adding beds is the opposite of what the passage suggests."),
(P2 + " Why did Nightingale use records and charts?",
 "To convince officials with evidence", ["To train new army surgeons", "To count the hospital's supplies", "To report soldiers who misbehaved"],
 "She used charts to persuade officials that clean conditions save lives."),
(P2 + " What can be inferred from the passage?",
 "Dirty conditions caused many deaths", ["Nightingale was trained as a surgeon", "Officials agreed with her at once", "Most soldiers died on the battlefield"],
 "The death rate fell sharply after the wards were cleaned, which implies the filth had been causing deaths. She had to persuade officials, so they did not agree at once."),
(P3 + " Where does the Aedes mosquito breed?",
 "In clean, standing water", ["In dirty, flowing canals", "In tall grass and bushes", "In damp, dark closets"],
 "The passage states that the mosquito breeds in clean, standing water such as water in old tires and vases."),
(P3 + " Why does treatment focus on rest and fluids?",
 "No medicine kills the virus", ["The illness is always mild", "Medicines are too expensive", "The virus dies within a day"],
 "The passage says that because no medicine kills the virus, treatment focuses on rest, fluids and watching for warning signs."),
(P3 + " Which is named as a warning sign of dengue?",
 "Bleeding gums", ["Itchy bites", "Dry cough", "Sore throat"],
 "Severe stomach pain and bleeding gums are the warning signs given in the passage."),
(P3 + " According to the passage, what is the best protection against dengue?",
 "Destroying mosquito breeding sites", ["Staying indoors in the afternoon", "Taking medicine before a bite", "Drinking plenty of clean water"],
 "The final sentence says the most effective protection is to search for and destroy the places where mosquitoes lay their eggs."),
(P4 + " What is the main idea of the passage?",
 "Sleep is needed for learning and health", ["Teenagers should stop using gadgets", "Studying all night improves memory", "Illness is caused by late bedtimes"],
 "The passage explains how sleep helps memory, reaction time and the body's defenses. Gadgets are mentioned only as one cause of lost sleep."),
(P4 + " What does the brain do during sleep?",
 "Sorts and stores the day's experiences", ["Rests and stops all activity", "Forgets what was studied that day", "Speeds up the body's reaction time"],
 "The passage says the brain sorts the day's experiences and stores what is worth keeping."),
(P4 + " Why do many teenagers get too little sleep?",
 "Late-night screen use", ["Too much homework", "Early morning classes", "Noisy neighborhoods"],
 "The passage gives late-night screen use as the reason many teenagers sleep far less than they need."),
(P4 + " Which advice does the passage support for the night before a long quiz?",
 "Study, then get a full night's sleep", ["Study all night without stopping", "Skip studying and sleep all day", "Review on a phone in bed until late"],
 "Students who sleep well after studying usually remember more than those who stay up all night."),
]
